# Pinned package-repo snapshot — Valve's official Steam Frame ("deckard") aarch64 Arch Linux port.
#
# Every snapshot/stripped row of rootfs/manifest.lock and installer/manifest.lock is installed from
# this repo, and build/builder.pin pins the SAME snapshot's system.rootfs.zst as the builder, so the
# pacman laying a root down comes from the snapshot it lays down.
#
# Tree: https://holo-packages.steamos.cloud/archlinux-deckard/archlinux/<snapshot>/<repo>/os/aarch64
# Each snapshot publishes core, extra (+ -debug), extra-archive, multilib, sources/, its own
# pacman.conf (only [core] and [extra], SigLevel = Optional — no detached signatures anywhere), and
# system.rootfs.zst. We enable the same two repos (rootfs/conf/pacman.conf).
#
# ALIASES — the directory names are not all frozen snapshots:
#   main, dev, builds, pipeline, tmp   moving CI aliases. Never pinned.
#   mash-YYYYMMDD                      the FIRST revision of a snapshot, and ALSO the alias that
#                                      follows .1, .2 … once they land. Measured on the preview
#                                      mirror 2026-07-26: mash-20251118 was byte-identical to .3.
#   mash-YYYYMMDD.N                    a frozen revision. Prefer one whenever it exists.
#   *.pvt / *-pvt                      a second publishing line, refused here. Measured 2026-09-23:
#                                      mash-20260305 is byte-identical (core.db, extra.db, rootfs
#                                      ETag) to mash-20260305.1.pvt, and mash-20260202 to .2.pvt —
#                                      the unsuffixed alias follows the newest .N.pvt. 20251118.3.pvt
#                                      carries the same 4560 package files as .3 (sha256 + builddate)
#                                      plus bootstrap repos. We pin the alias and let the lock hold it.
# An unsuffixed pin is accepted because the per-package sha256 in the locks is the real pin:
# rootfs/fetchlock.sh verifies every file, so a republish fails the build instead of drifting.
#
# Pin = last non-comment, non-blank line: a repo base URL. build/lib-pins.sh validates it (all
# stages source it) and the stages append /$repo/os/$arch.
# Bumping is deliberate: change this line AND build/builder.pin, `make relock`, review both locks.
#
# The previous pin, holo-core-aarch64-preview/mash-20251118.3, is a frozen public mirror of this
# tree's mash-20251118.3: core.db and extra.db are byte-identical on both hosts (checked 2026-09-23).
#
# mash-20260305 is UNSUFFIXED (no .1 published as of 2026-09-23). Measured 2026-09-23:
#   core.db            45288 bytes  2026-09-15  ETag 6aa963ee-b0e8
#   system.rootfs.zst  331490479 bytes  2026-09-15  ETag 6aa96e54-13c224af
# A different ETag on either means the alias moved to a .1: re-pin to that revision.
# .github/workflows/upstream-watch.yml (deckard-base) reads the core.db ETag from the line above
# and opens an issue when the served one differs — keep the `core.db … ETag <value>` shape.
https://holo-packages.steamos.cloud/archlinux-deckard/archlinux/mash-20260305
